  "id": "group-pressure",
  "term": "group pressure",
  "definition": "Group pressure is the influence a majority exerts that leads a person to change their beliefs or behaviour to match the group. This can happen because people want acceptance from others or because they treat the group as a reliable guide to what is correct.",
